$ trilium append meeting1 '<p>Action items</p>'
appended meeting1 +19 bytes: 68 → 87 bytes

$ trilium append meeting1 -f '$DIR/more.html' --top
appended meeting1 +11 bytes: 87 → 98 bytes

$ trilium append script1 'print('\''bye'\'')'
appended script1 +12 bytes: 12 → 24 bytes

$ trilium append script1 '# header' --top
appended script1 +9 bytes: 24 → 33 bytes

$ trilium append meeting1
stderr| error: no content given
stderr| hint: give the content as an argument, with -f FILE, or with -f - (stdin), e.g.:
stderr|       trilium append <note> "<p>text</p>"
stderr|       trilium append <note> -f body.html
exit: 2

$ trilium append meeting1 x -f '$DIR/more.html'
stderr| error: give the content only one way: as an argument, with -f FILE, or with -f - (stdin)
exit: 2

$ trilium append _options '<p>x</p>'
